# opt-doc-4 — Fix #3: response out-buffer overhaul (C side) — and an honest note on where Lean fits

Date: 2026-11-04 · Branch: `dev/optimize2` · Parent: opt-doc-3

## Correction to opt-doc-1

`x_out_json_escaped_str` + `grow` are **C (`runtime/abi.c`)**, not emitted asm —
the emitted code only calls them (3 call sites in `app_gen.s`). opt-doc-1's
classifier bucketed `x_*` names under "C runtime" but the prose called it the
"emitted-asm path"; the perf stack (`x_out_json_escaped_str → grow`) settled it.
The emitted layer itself stays <1% of hot CPU — consistent with its design role
(routing/parsing/serializing logic), with C services (crypto/JSON/db/transport)
carrying the heavy lifting.

## Changes (`runtime/abi.c`, `runtime/main.c`) — no Lean re-derive, no promotion gate

1. **Escape fast path**: the old loop called `x_out_mem`/`x_out_byte` (function
   call + `grow(o,1)` capacity check) *per byte*. New: bulk-scan the run of
   plain bytes (`>= 0x20`, not `"`/`\`), one `memcpy` per run; the per-byte
   switch only runs on escape bytes and writes directly after a single
   `grow(o,6)`. Contract byte-for-byte identical (42 goldens exercise escaped
   seed content; comment pins the contract).
2. **`x_out_int`**: `snprintf` → manual decimal (ids/counts on every row).
3. **Scratch OutBuf reuse**: `main.c` used `struct OutBuf out = {0}` +
   `free(out.base)` per request — the 256-byte initial `grow` ladder meant
   ~6 reallocs per feed response plus a malloc/free pair per request. Now a
   static 4 KiB scratch buffer is reused across requests (event loop is
   single-threaded; content fully rewritten per response; realloc growth
   persists in the global). Per-request allocation → zero on the steady path.

## Why not a Lean change here

The profiled cost lives in C services; the emitted layer is <1% of hot CPU.
Rewriting the serializer's call pattern inside the emitter (e.g. emitting
`x_out_reserve` calls per row) would re-derive `app_gen.s`, pay the
promotion gate, and buy ~nothing the scratch buffer doesn't already amortize.
Lean's leverage in this stack is proving app *logic* changes cheap and safe
(corpus + proofs), not micro-optimizing C helper internals. Recorded as a
deliberate decision.

